  "source_review": [
    "Default TextInput blur policy restored; Tab commits typed value and ends editing without submitting. Pointer Save exposes committed typed value and preserves clicked action identity.",
    "Submission checks addressed Intent::Binding resolved through the actual input Bindings table to TextCmd::Commit, not raw Enter. It excludes simultaneous FocusOut, so blur commits do not become primary submission.",
    "TextInput bindings currently ignore BindingState and return the same BINDINGS used by update_target, so helper resolution matches actual input command handling.",
    "Configured primary remains limited to enabled effective actions; missing/disabled/truncated/empty cases fail closed. Focused alternatives Enter/Space and custom action chords retain own keys.",
    "Acknowledgement branch and secret input configuration are unchanged by this correction; existing acknowledgement tests included in165 native pass.",
    "Additive private helper; no public signature/layout removal, second runtime, application imports, reference assets or painter bypasses.",
    "Public standalone Dialog consumer compiles through Nextest list; zero tests in example are compilation evidence only."
  ],
